was known about their dynamics. In this work we investigate the stability of autonomous and periodic NRE of the type  \nx(t) = f(t)x(t − τ)  \nfrom a theoretical point of view, performing numerical experiments both to exemplify our findings and to guide our investigation. Our numerical approach is based on the pseudospectral collocation technique of [2, 3] for discretizing monodromy operators and computing Floquet multipliers, although a proof of Floquet theory for NRE is currently lacking.\n\n## References\n\n[1] O. Diekmann, S. M. Verduyn Lunel, *Twin semigroups and delay equations*, J. Differential Equations, 286 (2021), pp. 332–410.\n\n[2] D. Breda, D. Liessi, *Approximation of eigenvalues of evolution operators for linear renewal equations*, SIAM J. Numer. Anal., 56 (2018), pp. 1456–1481.\n\n[3] D. Breda, D. Liessi, R. Vermiglio, *Piecewise discretization of monodromy operators of delay equations on adapted meshes*, J. Comput. Dyn., 9 (2022), pp. 103–121.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLibrary · teal-sea (https://zeta.teal-sea.com/library.html)\nciteturn7search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: yesterday; Crawled: today; #### Central logarithmic moments, 2026-10-02 ... #### The same complete spectrum can hide different simple-point counts ... read · 1,718 words · hunts/cycle_moments/FINITE-THEOREM.md ... Started 2026-09-05 under the operator's instruction to pursue substantive mathematical research with the available provers and compute resources.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Spectra of evolution operators of a class of neutral renewal equations: theoretical and numerical aspects (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/368159579_Spectra_of_evolution_operators_of_a_class_of_neutral_renewal_equations_theoretical_and_numerical_aspects)\nciteturn7search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.8 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; , with some points of the spectrum bein